cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use CausalRLBreaker in your research, please cite this work."

title: "CausalRLBreaker: Security Testing of Large Language Models via Causal Reinforcement Learning"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Zeinaliashtiyani"
    given-names: "Parisa"

version: "1.0.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/parisazeynaly/Security-Testing-of-Large-Language-Models-via-Reinforcement-Learning"

url: "https://github.com/parisazeynaly/Security-Testing-of-Large-Language-Models-via-Reinforcement-Learning"

license: "Apache-2.0"

abstract: >
  CausalRLBreaker is a research framework for automated security testing
  of large language models using causal reinforcement learning. The
  framework integrates causal state representations, structural causal
  modeling, causal reward shaping, and intervention-guided reinforcement
  learning for black-box LLM security evaluation.

keywords:
  - "large language models"
  - "LLM security"
  - "AI security"
  - "red teaming"
  - "causal machine learning"
  - "causal reinforcement learning"
  - "reinforcement learning"
  - "structural causal models"
  - "causal discovery"
  - "PPO"
